WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
Christians believe that
God's grace is a gift.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.010
Nobody can earn it.

3
00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:10.360
But in 1937 a German pastor warned
that grace could become cheap:

4
00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.780
the deadly enemy of the Church.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:18.210
His name was Dietrich Bonhoeffer, and
his book was The Cost of Discipleship.

6
00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:20.740
How can a free gift be cheap?

7
00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.730
And what could make it costly?

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.480
In this mission, you'll read the
Gospel texts behind his book:

9
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:30.490
a call, a cross, and
treasure hidden in a field.

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.550
Then you'll weigh up whether Bonhoeffer
puts too much weight on suffering,

11
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.180
and whether he still matters today.

12
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:42.450
Your mission: find out what Bonhoeffer
meant by cheap grace and costly grace.
